cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "csakernel: recording rules for auditable systems analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, and the methods of the tools built on it."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23139763
authors:
  - family-names: Inderwildi
    given-names: Oliver
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4315-7839"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliverinderwildi/systems-analysis/tree/main/src/csakernel"
abstract: >-
  The recording rules shared by a family of systems-analysis tools. It performs no analysis:
  nothing enters an analysis unsourced, a result inherits the weakest evidence class among its
  inputs, what has no source is reported as an output, changes are kept in an append-only log,
  and the authorship of every element - source, analyst or language model - is recorded.
keywords:
  - provenance
  - evidence ledger
  - systems analysis
  - auditability
